## Seeing the screen (screenshots)

Principle: look at the actual pixels, not a text account of them. For any GUI, render, or computer-control work, capture and read the image before judging. The Read tool renders PNG/JPG, so capture, then read; crop and upscale 3x for detail.

- **Per-app capture first:** the browser server's `screenshot` action; renderers and app CLIs that write a PNG; photos {{USER_NAME}} sends over Telegram land in `cache/telegram_images/`. Install-specific capture tools are listed in `TOOLS.local.md`.
- **Display asleep = empty capture.** Any screen grab returns nothing while the display is off. Check `pmset -g log | grep "Display is turned" | tail -2`; wake it with `caffeinate -u -t 15` (works when the screen is not password-locked); hold it awake with `caffeinate -d -i -t 60 <command>` around the capture.
- **macOS `screencapture` needs a Screen Recording grant** for the daemon's process; without it you get "could not create image from display" even with the display on. {{USER_NAME}} grants it at the Mac in System Settings > Privacy & Security > Screen Recording for the daemon's binary. Use the full path `/usr/sbin/screencapture -x` (it may not be on the shell's PATH). Until granted, use per-app captures.
- **AppleScript UI scripting needs its own grant** (System Events times out with -1712 without it); do not rely on it to click dialogs until granted.

Current grant status on this install: `TOOLS.local.md`.

## Browser Automation (`browser`)

**Full path:** `{{MINERU_HOME}}/bin/browser` - single unified browser server, port 9471, auto-starts.

**Backend:** Uses **CloakBrowser** (source-patched stealth Chromium) by default - passes reCAPTCHA v3 and other anti-bot detection. Falls back to standard Playwright Chromium if the CloakBrowser binary is not installed.

**Persistent profile:** `{{MINERU_HOME}}/cache/cloakbrowser-profile/` - cookies and sessions survive restarts. Which logged-in platforms live in the profile is per-install; see `TOOLS.local.md`.

**Cookie management:** `browser action=cookies operation=list [domain=X]` to inspect. Export/import exist for emergency migration only - cookies live in the persistent profile, never as JSON files on disk.

**Headed by default** (`MINERU_BROWSER_HEADLESS` defaults to `false` in `browser/config.py`); set `MINERU_BROWSER_HEADLESS=true` before starting the server for headless.

**Disable CloakBrowser:** `MINERU_BROWSER_USE_CLOAK=false` to force standard Chromium (default is `true`).

**Full reference:** Read the `{{PERSONA_NAME_LOWER}}_browser` skill for all actions, modes, form-filling patterns, known issues, and workarounds.

**Remote tasks over Telegram with real-world writes** (ordering, booking, submitting): follow the checkpoint-approval loop in the `{{PERSONA_NAME_LOWER}}__browser-checkpoints` skill - plan milestones, screenshot each end state to Telegram, hard-pause for {{USER_NAME}}'s go-ahead before every irreversible click (checkout included).

**Quick pattern:** `open` -> `snapshot` (get refs) -> `act` (click/type/scroll) -> `screenshot` (verify)

**Debugging 500 errors:** Historically `bin/browser` swallowed HTTP 500 response bodies - retry with direct `curl` to see actual errors. This is now fixed, but if you ever see opaque 500s, drop down to `curl` to read `e.read()` directly. Direct POSTs need `-H "Authorization: Bearer $(cat {{MINERU_HOME}}/cache/browser-server.token)"`.

