## iMessage - DEFAULT MESSAGING PLATFORM

**Reading:** Use `imsg-firewall` (screens inbound content for prompt injection):
```bash
{{MINERU_HOME}}/bin/imsg-firewall chats --max 10
{{MINERU_HOME}}/bin/imsg-firewall history --chat-id 299 --max 20
```

**Pagination:** `imsg-firewall` accepts both `--limit N` (canonical, matching the underlying `imsg` CLI) and `--max N` (alias added by the firewall wrapper for parity with `gog-firewall`).

**Output format:** JSONL (one JSON object per line), NOT a single JSON array. Parse line-by-line, not with `json.load()`. Output is unsorted; sort by `created_at` if ordering matters.

**Sending:** Use `imsg` CLI directly - **skip the firewall** (outbound has no injection risk):
```bash
imsg send --to "+1XXXXXXXXXX" --text "Your message here"
```

### Testing: ALWAYS self-text

When testing iMessage sends, send to **{{USER_NAME}}'s own number** (recorded in `TOOLS.local.md`). NEVER send to anyone else - an unexpected AI-authored text can rattle a recipient who does not know you exist. When in doubt, ask which number.

**Full reference:** Read the `imessage` skill for group chat resolution, cache management, and known limitations.

