## Apple Notes (`memo`)

**Full path:** `/opt/homebrew/bin/memo` (Python CLI, Homebrew-installed)

**`memo` is SLOW** - it is Python + AppleScript IPC to Notes.app. Every command takes 20-45 seconds. Always use long timeouts:

```bash
# Always pass a Bash timeout of at least 60000 ms
memo notes -f "Folder Name"    # List notes in folder
memo notes -fl                 # List all folders
memo notes                     # List all notes (very slow with many notes)
```

Which folders exist on this install lives in `TOOLS.local.md`.

**Reading note content:** `memo` does not have a direct "read note by name" command. For reading content, use AppleScript:
```bash
osascript -e '
tell application "Notes"
    set theNote to first note in folder "FolderName" whose name is "NoteName"
    return plaintext of theNote
end tell'
```

